# {{ .prefix }}-reviewing-plan

## When this skill fires

Terminal step of `{{ .prefix }}-writing-plans`, and the ordinary freshness owner after a linked ADR changes. For a new plan it runs before the first commit against an explicit path and selected working-tree snapshot. For an existing Proposed plan it runs after the amended ADR's review settles. The `plan-reviewer` subagent is a report-only judge: it reads the plan and every ADR resolved from parsed plan-level `adrs:`, runs all universal lenses, classifies each finding as mechanical / reasoned / user-decision, and returns a findings digest. This skill dispatches that agent, applies the fixes, runs a single verify pass, gates on user-decision findings, and chains to the next node.

This full review owns linked-authority freshness; it does not select plans or ADRs by modification time, session implication, or an assumed one-to-one relationship.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:include review-remediation-autonomy -->

## Procedure

This skill may run without an effort. If continuity independently fired, validate the fixed effort identity and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`, preserve one user-managed writer, and give the report-only reviewer that context read-only; otherwise omit effort and memory fields. If changed facts newly make continuity useful, invoke `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` before further mutation. Repository sources, the plan, and current-state documentation remain authoritative, and standalone memory is forbidden.

<!-- awf:section procedure -->
1. **Identify the plan path and snapshot.** Require the caller's explicit uncommitted plan path and selected working-tree snapshot for a new draft, or an explicit existing plan path and selected snapshot for freshness. For a new draft, review the uncommitted snapshot. For freshness after ADR review, consume the deterministic linked-plan paths reported by the explicit ADR context result and invoke this workflow separately for every linked plan whose parsed status remains `Proposed`. Do not infer a most-recent file, use modification time or session implication, silently substitute HEAD, or omit a linked Proposed plan.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section artifact-path-detection -->
2. **Snapshot and authority detail.** Read the plan from the selected working-tree snapshot and resolve every ADR identity in its parsed plan-level `adrs:` set. Refuse an absent path, ambiguous snapshot, unresolved ADR, or incomplete linked-ADR set. When implementation has started, inventory completed phases against the changed ADR, identify every affected phase, and require renewed implementation assurance for affected landed work before progression.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section dispatch-subagent -->
{{ if .targetSubagentTools }}3. **Call `subagent_review` with `kind: "plan"`.** Put the complete reviewer brief in `task`; Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value. Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md. The brief must include:
{{ else }}3. **Dispatch the `plan-reviewer` subagent.** Provide it a brief that includes the following. Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable. Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md.
{{ end }}   - The absolute plan path and selected working-tree snapshot, with an explicit instruction to review that snapshot rather than HEAD; identify the path as uncommitted only for a new precommit draft. When present, include the effort slug and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md` read-only.
   - Every user-provenance decision-log entry from the effort memory pasted verbatim, including whatever `Record:` blocks exist, so the consensus-adherence check can run; a log without user entries omits the paste and leaves that check idle.
   - The declared per-phase ownership, phase context, closing subjects, and any helper partitions alongside created/modified paths, so review assesses the same phase boundary.
   - The instruction to run in full mode (all universal lenses), read every ADR resolved from the plan's parsed `adrs:` set, and reject modification-time or session-inferred authority.
   - When a linked ADR changed after implementation started, the completed-phase inventory, affected phases, and assurance that must be renewed before progression.
   - The affected context instruction: collect every task-level `Paths:` entry plus exact repository paths named in task titles and bodies, deduplicate the resolved set, and direct the reviewer to run `awf context --show invariants --show all-rules --show evidence --show pending <those paths>` itself so the doc-currency and convention-alignment lenses receive the non-direct invariant summaries, additional topic rules, backing evidence, and pending changes they need without unrelated facets. Do not infer a path from vague prose. Pass the resolved paths, not pasted packet output.
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->
   - The instruction to return findings as `[{focus, severity, location, issue, suggested_fix, classification}]`.

   The reviewer handles lens application and finding classification, and returns the digest. Fix application and the verify pass are this skill's job (steps below). Do not ask the reviewer to edit, commit, or re-review.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section classify-route-findings -->
4. **Surface the digest, then route the findings.** Display the digest the `plan-reviewer` agent returns to the user. Then route the classified findings by classification kind, not severity:
   - **mechanical**: this skill applies directly.
   - **reasoned**: this skill applies with a one-line rationale.
   - **user-decision**: present to the user with the cited affected authority and wait.
   A correction that would contradict any linked ADR is never applied to the plan: return first to ADR amendment and ordinary ADR review, then start a fresh ordinary plan review after that authority settles.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section apply-fixes-commit -->
5. **Settle the plan and commit once.** Apply mechanical fixes directly without a durable ledger. Record substantive reasoned or user-decided findings and dispositions in plan Notes. For a new draft, after the optional single verify pass stage and gate the settled draft and create one initial plan commit. Later substantive corrections remain separate commits, including freshness corrections; every actual commit uses staged checks and the full gate.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section re-review-loop -->
6. **Verify pass.** A round that applied no fixes dispatches no verify pass, and a fix round whose applied fixes are all classified `mechanical` skips it, recording the skip and its ground in the summary presented at the check-in. When at least one applied fix is classified `reasoned` or was applied under a `user-decision` ruling, {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}call `subagent_review` exactly once with `kind: "plan"` and a verify brief in `task`. Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value. Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md.{{ else }}dispatch exactly one fresh `plan-reviewer` verify pass. Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable. Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md.{{ end }} This pass confirms the fixes resolved the findings without new issues. Diagnose every residual finding under the authority-guided remediation boundary above, apply the authority-preserving mechanical and reasoned residual corrections, and report their disposition. Stop only for a residual finding that remains a true user decision, and dispatch no further same-artifact review pass.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section hand-off -->
7. **Hand off after review settles.** Once the settled initial or freshness review converges, proceed directly to the target-native inline or subagent-driven execution skill according to each phase's declared ownership. If implementation had started, do not progress until every affected completed phase has renewed assurance.

<!-- awf:include checkpoint-routine -->
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section notes -->
## Notes

- If the user asks to skip review, comply but warn that a chain step is being skipped.
- See `{{ .layout.workflowRef }}` for full plan lifecycle rules and the canonical workflow chain.
- For V2 ADR work, require tasks to assign declared operations to pair-atomic batches and account for Applied, Remaining, and Canceled partitions.
- For plan-v2, require retained pending ADR slugs, V4 stable `decision:` selectors, and frozen `#N` selectors only for pre-V4 records. Check Applying and Context omission-not-empty semantics, every plan-level Decision's substantive Applying assignment, and every DoD item's final Completes owner; Proposed coverage notes are advisory and historical Decision prose never replaces current-state authority.
- The `plan-reviewer` is one lens-diverse subagent; this skill does not fan out per-lens subagents or specify per-lens model routing.
- The reviewer remains report-only; draft settlement is parent-owned and substantive dispositions remain in Notes.
<!-- awf:end -->
